ice on the back  so that you can adjust backwards and  forwards  really easily i love this thing it's  great the other thing a lot of you are  going to want to check out is the oculus  link cable i just got a new one of these  um and it basically connects the oculus  quest 2 to a pc i recommend this more  for when you're not working out but it  basically takes the quest to  and turns it into  a vr headset  that's powered by a pc it's fantastic it  is a  sleek little cable but let's open her up  anyway  voila  a cable so obviously a really important  thing about this is the length um for  anyone who wants to connect it to a pc  it's five meters so it's going to be  very easy for you to have your oculus  plugged in and connected to your pc  without worrying about what the chord is  doing and it's pretty much exactly as  simple as you would think that it is you  plug  one part into the side of your quest and  one part into your pc  that's it  it does also come with um which i'm a  very big fan of i feel like i always get  screwed when people don't do this this  guy right here this little velcro strap  that allows you to properly strap the  cable to the side of your quest too so  that when you're playing it's directly  connected basically so you know exactly  where the cable is you know it's  attached to your head at all times that  you are controlling what the cable is  doing it's pretty handy stuff when  you're in vr so there you have it i just  wanted to give you guys a little bit  more insight to working out with an  oculus quest 2  give everybody an update on how things  are going with me there and just show  that i feel like it really genuinely can  be very fun  you can own a gym a boxing ring a dance  studio and even a climbing wall all  inside of an oculus quest 2. though  supernatural vr  is the game that tends to consistently  burn the most calories for me there are  a whole bunch of other fitness games  that i also play that i have spoken  about on the channe